{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789386862,"nonce":"E1wqsgfGZ9Ylc6uPGVoQtwtc+dk=","title":"Code only an error path reaches is compiled on its first call","message":"Of the 104 functions a ten-line Python kernel compiled, about seventy\nwere exception machinery: every exception class's constructor and\nunboxer, the traceback reporter and the repr functions it can reach,\nthe raise hooks. All of it was lowered, optimised and handed to\nCranelift on every run, ~9 ms of codegen and a similar share of the\noptimisers, for code a correct program never executes.\n\nNow (`dce::cold_only_function_ids`): from the declared entry points,\ndirect calls are followed except into a function marked cold, so\nwhatever only cold code reaches is cold-only. A function whose address\nis taken, that is called by name, or that the host may enter is pinned\nhot. Cold-only functions are left as lowered (the optimisers skip\nthem), and codegen emits a stub per function instead of the body: the\nstub calls `__zyntax_lazy_compile(bead_id)` and then the entry it gets\nwith its own arguments. Calls to such a function go through its reload\ncell, which holds the stub until the runtime's lazy compiler\n(`TieredBackend::install_lazy_compiler`) optimises all the cold bodies\ntogether, once, compiles the one asked for at tier 0, and publishes\nits entry into the cell. `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_LAZY_COLD=1` compiles\neverything up front; `ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY=1` prints what is hot and why.\nNot under hot reload, whose cells are spoken for.\n\nTwo frontend changes make the error paths cold in the first place: the\nuncaught-exception report is a cold library function (`zb_uncaught`)\nrather than code inlined into `__main__`, and a raise the lowering\nemits calls a cold `py$raise$Class(message)` that builds the instance\nand leaves it pending, so a raise block ends in a cold call and the\ninliner and the laziness both read it as an error path.\n\nmandelbrot_strip compile 30 to 18 ms (Cranelift 8.7 to 2.3, the\noptimisers 12 to 6); fib 15.5; a loop raising 200k exceptions 47 to\n35 ms, since the raise path is now a call rather than inlined\nconstruction.","files":null}]}